# Whitelist .gitignore -- ignore everything, then allow only what should ship.
# New notes and drafts stay untracked by default, which is the point: nothing
# reaches the remote unless it is named here.

# 1. ignore every file
*

# 2. but let git descend into directories, so the rules below can match inside
!*/

# 3. scripts, documents and the web paper
!.gitignore
!*.md
!*.MD
!*.py
!*.qmd
!*.yml
!*.scss
!*.js
!publish/**

# 4. raw data: never committed -- large, and all of it is publicly downloadable.
#    Ship the download instructions instead.
data_raw/*
!data_raw/README.md

# 5. output: what the web paper draws its figures from, nothing else. A reader
#    who downloads the raw data reproduces everything else with the scripts.
#    The PDF's static figures (output/figures/) are printed when the PDF is
#    rendered and are not stored.
output/*
# Every occupation's score on the six axes, and every variable's loading on
# them: the axes themselves.
!output/rotated_axes.csv
!output/rotated_loadings.csv
# Figure 6.2 is drawn from this. It holds occupation-level shares aggregated
# from the IPUMS extract, not the microdata, which stays in data_raw/.
!output/acs_young_share.csv
!assets/*.png

# 6. junk
__pycache__/
.ipynb_checkpoints/
.DS_Store
reports/
.idea/
# Quarto build output. The last two lines are the exact form Quarto looks
# for, so keeping them here stops it appending them on every render.
_site/
.quarto/
/.quarto/
**/*.quarto_ipynb